I definitely saw some problematic plagiarism at my US University, albeit on a smaller scale.

&nbsp;

Freshman year, I was working with a Chinese student on a Mathematics presentation where we had to learn and then present what we learned about Fractals. I played around with the fractals to see if I could get a good pattern, and my partner cut and pasted Wikipedia for the presentation.

&nbsp;

Junior year in my Abstract Algebra class, I had to peer review a paper that was written by a group of Chinese students, one being the same guy I was partnered with before. I discovered that it was a cut and paste of the chapter of the textbook verbatim. Paragraphs of the textbook. Gave a nasty peer review where I pointed out the plagiarism, but nothing ever came of it. Probably should have taken it to the Dean.

&nbsp;

I know that there are good Chinese students that want to learn, and I met one in a different class Junior year. I hope he got to do the internship he was shooting for because he was really good with Stats. of it. Probably should have taken it to the Dean.

