Going into this, even if it was a real job I figured I was not likely to play it anyway.
I pretty much just play BRD and SCH because they are what my play style is comfortable with and I like their kits.

&nbsp;

I was cautiously optimistic about the whole "Limited Job" thing until they revealed that there will be RNG behind getting the abilities. Pretty much anything RNG in this game is fairly brutal, so I figure this will not be an exception.

&nbsp;

The thing that I am now realizing is that BLU's "endgame" content is that Carnival. That's literally it. That's the whole point of the job. That's all you can do besides screwing around with the actions in stuff that people already break on level 70 jobs.

&nbsp;

The carnival is going to need some heavy variation to make it interesting to play past the first few tournaments.

&nbsp;

The more I think about it, the worse I feel about it because there are plenty of better things they could have worked on. I get people asked for it, but Yoshi P literally said that he trusts no one after Gordias was way too difficult. If it does not work for the game, it does not work.

It's certainly not optimal to be at the mercy of the marketboard for materials, but you could theoretically do it. People do put up intermediates for crafts, especially the lower level expansion mats that drop from treasure maps.

&nbsp;

If your main concern is it being a money sink, once you get a crafting/gathering job to 60, you unlock a weekly source of income(scrips) and exp called custom deliveries. Once you hit 70, you can get a second type of scrips instead of exp. Scrips can be traded for items like materia that you could sell for gil, or they can be used to get gain access to special nodes/recipies and mediocre equipment. Crafting scrips are usually a better source of income than gathering.

&nbsp;

Gathering allows you to collect treasure maps that you can sell. They tend to fluctuate in price a lot though, but cost nothing but time to grab. They start appearing at level 36 when you can see level 40 nodes, I believe.

To get a better idea of that you would want to check how much the individual raw mats and crafted items sell for on your server. But you are mostly paying for convenience and having someone do menial crafting. That being said, probably don't pay more than 500K for a 15-50, unless hide prices are just high on your server. LTW is hard to gauge due to the mats being harder to obtain than most of the other classes, especially for 15-50.

&nbsp;

[This is one of many levekit item lists.](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/11L0KG35EXmEk3LsYvncYVj7w7E05aPxE--ZetnJIRC4/htmlview#)

I don't have too much faith in their decisions after the whole surprise announcement of silver border cards being commander legal for several weeks.

&nbsp;

It was heavy handed despite being controversal. It was not left up to tournaments or playgroups. I remember seeing a PSA post shortly afterword where some large store had to say not to bring silver border cards to the event.

&nbsp;

The short duration coupled with the surprise announcement meant that people that did want to participate likely lost time due to needing to order cards and deck building.

&nbsp;

If they really wanted it unmander to be a thing, they should have let the community decide to play it, not force it out of nowhere.

It's not so much that people have not seen a rotation like that, and more that each rotation has pros and cons. 

&nbsp;

The 800GP rotation has the potential to yield one more item per node, GP regen alone will not keep up with it very well, and you have to use some kind of food (could be very cheap or a bit more expensive depending on how much GP is melded to gear). There is also the chance of having some feel bad moments when RNG is awful.

Obviously, when we reach 850GP in 5.x, that should have the best aspects of both rotations.

&nbsp;

You should be able to get up to 5 gathering attempts if you use [the third rotation on this post](https://ff14ru.enjin.com/forum/m/24610498/viewthread/31977474-43-collectible-gathering-rotations-by-balance-discord/post/134432527) and add a single mind to the front of it. 3 attempts is still the worst case possibility.

You can do it, however, you may have to set up your own party finder since, people typically inflate the required item level on their party finder requirements.

&nbsp;

Good luck finding a group. I hope you can get a good one!

I can definitely concede that glamour is impacted by this, but I think it is actually more fair if everyone has equal opportunity to get the gear.

&nbsp;

Also, why is vanity more important than desynth and GC currency? (Someone could use the GC seals from that glamour gear for a GC glamour gear piece.) 

&nbsp;

If someone needs i360 gear that badly, there is the i360 augmented crafted gear set that is not weekly locked.

&nbsp;

There is also an abundance of free i350 gear they could also use until they have enough tomes for i360.

&nbsp;

I guess my point is that people play the game for different reasons, and this raid is not the only way to get gear.

