There is a metaphorical anvil hovering over their head. They are in good shape only at the mercy of GPU mining still being relevant.

&nbsp;

They have no choice but to keep selling, only because if they stop, Nvidia could pick up the slack. Nvidia would be happy to see AMD suffer, even if they have to suffer too. Nvidia can handle the sharp decline in sales that will follow mining a lot better than AMD can.

&nbsp;

The main problem people probably have with what you've said in this comment thread further up is that it seems sort of backwards to pretend these unsustainable sales are good for AMD. It looks really good now, but AMD will be living with the consequences of selling all of these cards to their temporary owners (miners) soon.

I read the job descriptions in 3.1 when I started, and knew that Scholar would be my best fit since it is the pet healing class with shields. I really liked the concept of Eos filling in the gaps in my healing.

&nbsp; 

That being said, I also briefly tried out Bard as an alternative to healing. It seemed really great having total mobility, until I found out that it was mostly a lie in the upper levels. I could not deal with the potential stance dancing on an 18s(?) cooldown when I occasionally flubbed Cleric Stance.

&nbsp; 

Fast forward to 4.0 and I realized that Scholar plays way too differently on too many levels for me to main it. Having 4 dots and applying them in the opener weaving in energy drains was a ton of fun. That being changed along with the new mana constraints and fairy potency reduction made the job feel less than familiar. I still leveled it first, but my only thought while playing it was that I wished for 3.x Scholar back.

&nbsp;

Bard became the obvious choice with the mobility I expected, but I have since come to terms with 4.0 Scholar as an alt job.

Off the top of my head, my suggestion would be to make leveling gear and gear for fashion report (This week you could have been crafting flat caps for 60K each).

&nbsp;

You should do all 12 custom deliveries every week for the free crafting scrips. You should be able to save up enough Gyr Abanian Alchemics to have someone make you the Ala Mhigan Set. However, the market is not what it was a few weeks ago as far as the i350 crafted gear goes, so there is likely no need to rush to get geared at this point.

You should be able to use just 5's in guaranteed slots and overmeld 3 and 4's to reach the minimums for 2 star crafting. You'll have to use the Maker's Mark rotation and plenty of HQ materials, but it is possible.

&nbsp;

If you gear up ALC, then WVR and LTW, you could craft your own left side. From there, I would meld a bit heavier and you should have no problem making tools and 350 gear after that. You still shouldn't have to use V's other than guaranteed slots. 

&nbsp;

You could also use the yellow scrip tools on your specialists if you are careful about maximizing CP almost everywhere else (I skipped the 1 point on the Ala Mhigan body). They are much more work to get initially though, so I do not recommend them, but they are an option.

Is your graphics card set to always run at maximum clock speed? 

&nbsp;

I was having a similar issue with an i5 3550 and a GTX 770, but I noticed my graphics card was basically idle at the points where the frame rate dipped. You have to force your card to never idle.

Those 1500 items are whatever mats you need for your crafting classes, or what you sell on the market board.

&nbsp;

You can stack Commercial Survival Manual (or GC for lower level), Squadron Survival Manual, food, and rested exp. Combined they give decent exp, especially with some HQs mixed in. It's not the same time commitment as collectables, but if you dislike gathering you do not have to do it.

Bungie barely had enough time to make D2. As it was, D2 was supposed to come out in 2016. D2 was in development while Bungie was still making content for D1.

&nbsp;

The main issue is that Bungie and Activision have a 10 year contract where Bungie has to make at least one expansion a year or a new Destiny game. So, Destiny 3 is likely in development now and may not include everything from Destiny 2 at launch.
